{"id": "EUVD-2026-59552", "enisaUuid": "6920c32c-c9d9-3ffb-8edb-0ba5fc63d68d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nOPP: Fix race between OPP addition and lookup\n\nA race exists between dev_pm_opp_add_dynamic() and\ndev_pm_opp_find_freq_exact():\n\n  CPU0 (add)                          CPU1 (lookup)\n  -------------------------------     ------------------------------\n  _opp_add()\n    mutex_lock()\n    list_add(&new_opp->node, head)\n    mutex_unlock()                    _opp_table_find_key()\n                                        mutex_lock()\n                                        dev_pm_opp_get(opp)\n                                          kref_get()\n                                        mutex_unlock()\n    kref_init(&new_opp->kref)\n                                      dev_pm_opp_put()\n                                        kref_put_mutex()\n\nThe newly added OPP is inserted into the list before its kref is\ninitialized. A concurrent lookup can find this OPP and increment its\nreference count while it is still uninitialized, leading to refcount\ncorruption and a potential premature free.\n\nFix this by initializing ->kref and ->opp_table before making the OPP\nvisible via list_add(). This ensures any concurrent lookup observes a\nfully initialized object.\n\n[ Viresh: Updated commit log ]", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:59:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:38", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/932ebfad767be1395946cbc1727a7c38eeee3d24", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1946ea2f6b3ec00e313c78e83fc196f1f6aba2a9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46696b0b2123475d7f95909435c09808fc5ffd23", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb75bd7d9ae7672034f73ce67a57e6ac89bb39e5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5e1cc9a284bff2510981643a5bca4bc4c21b81a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5fpw-5c2c-j4pp", "CVE-2026-74405"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "26eeb381-40f9-33df-9a44-3d9df556072b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "36bf91b8-1528-334a-ac40-c194b5fad854", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "3aac01c7-75ac-394f-85ae-8a9e18be53fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "5ab2039c-864c-3986-b915-79e9c53f5cbe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7034764a1e4a6edbb60914e89aad8384e3fe5d17 <46696b0b2123475d7f95909435c09808fc5ffd23"}, {"id": "7a69f368-2305-3c2a-8d3f-87fc16acb5b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "8178e2be-4220-391a-adf5-df0c784ae977", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7034764a1e4a6edbb60914e89aad8384e3fe5d17 <1946ea2f6b3ec00e313c78e83fc196f1f6aba2a9"}, {"id": "b10be7ae-f83e-3dca-86fd-5dc01cf452a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b165a005-37b3-37ac-a76c-a095cd719a95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7034764a1e4a6edbb60914e89aad8384e3fe5d17 <bb75bd7d9ae7672034f73ce67a57e6ac89bb39e5"}, {"id": "b3649f25-6df7-3aff-a5cc-6290d15328ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7034764a1e4a6edbb60914e89aad8384e3fe5d17 <f5e1cc9a284bff2510981643a5bca4bc4c21b81a"}, {"id": "c905275a-19f6-39a9-8dbc-b4ca1e54ae81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "f53d6fb4-a6a6-3f53-a870-1549ca7d3233", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.11"}, {"id": "f84c7eae-95ed-34da-919e-6e4381d9678c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"nam